  "prompt": "The UK team reports in pounds. For the subscriptions billed in GBP, give each month's movements in 2025 (event_date from 1 January to 31 December 2025): new, expansion, reactivation, contraction and churn MRR in pounds, signed as in mrr_delta_local. Each event's event_type names its movement (new, expansion, contraction, churn or reactivation); a reactivation is an account coming back after it churned, never new MRR. Leave out the opening events: they carry the MRR subscriptions already had when the data starts on 1 January 2024. Count an event in the month of its event_date. A kind with no event that month shows 0. Return six columns, in this order: month_start (the first day of the month), new_mrr, expansion_mrr, reactivation_mrr, contraction_mrr and churn_mrr. Return one row for each month with at least one GBP movement event. Any row order is fine.",
